---
---

<section id="story" style="background:var(--cu-cream);position:relative;overflow:hidden;">
  <div class="container-wide">
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.05fr 0.95fr;gap:80px;align-items:center;">
      <!-- Left: long-form story -->
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow"><span class="tick"></span>The story · How I got here</div>
        <h2 class="section-title" style="max-width:580px;">
          I grew up obsessed with animals. <span style="color:var(--cu-gold);">It never went away.</span>
        </h2>

        <div style="font:500 17px var(--font-sans);color:var(--fg2);line-height:1.75;max-width:580px;">
          <p style="margin:0 0 20px;">
            My first pet was a hamster named Emily. I was probably eight years old,
            and I remember sitting and just <em>watching</em> her — trying to figure out
            what she wanted. That instinct, paying real attention to an animal instead
            of forcing them into a box, has been with me ever since.
          </p>
          <p style="margin:0 0 20px;">
            Dog training found me later. The moment I knew I was hooked: I met
            an eight-month-old puppy who was calm, attentive, and confident
            around strangers. Not a unicorn dog — a well-trained one. I spent
            the next decade chasing how to do that for other people's dogs.
          </p>
          <p style="margin:0 0 20px;">
            After ten years running boards-and-trains for other companies, I
            opened my own training business in 2018. The original name was
            Aninanny; eventually I rebranded it to Canine University because
            what I'm really teaching is humans — your dog is the easy part.
          </p>
          <p style="margin:0;">
            Today I work alongside my junior trainer Jayden out of our home
            base in Sunrise, Florida — covering Broward County for private
            lessons, with board &amp; train clients living in our home for two
            to three weeks at a time.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Right: photo collage -->
      <div class="about-collage" style="position:relative;height:680px;">
        <div class="photo-frame tilt-l about-collage-main" style="position:absolute;top:30px;left:0;width:380px;height:480px;z-index:2;">
          <img src="/assets/brianna.jpg" alt="Brianna Alamo, founder and lead trainer" />
        </div>

        <div class="photo-frame tilt-r about-collage-second" style="position:absolute;bottom:0;right:0;width:300px;height:340px;z-index:3;">
          <img src="/assets/training-session.jpg" alt="Brianna training a dog" />
        </div>

        <!-- Founded 2018 badge -->
        <div class="floaty about-collage-badge" style="position:absolute;top:0;right:60px;z-index:4;width:130px;height:130px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--cu-gold);color:var(--cu-navy);display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;box-shadow:var(--shadow-xl);">
          <div style="font:900 12px var(--font-sans);letter-spacing:0.18em;text-transform:uppercase;opacity:0.7;">Est.</div>
          <div style="font:900 32px var(--font-display);line-height:1;margin-top:4px;">2018</div>
        </div>

        <!-- Pull quote -->
        <div class="about-collage-quote" style="position:absolute;bottom:110px;left:30px;z-index:5;background:var(--cu-navy);color:#fff;padding:18px 22px;border-radius:18px;box-shadow:var(--shadow-xl);max-width:280px;">
          <div style="font:600 14px var(--font-sans);line-height:1.5;font-style:italic;">
            "Your dog already knows what they want. I just help you two agree on the rules."
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
